                    {
                        "sense_id": "c5cfa50e-35ab-343b-bdb8-9ec075d89186",
                        "entry_id": "355b619a-4a14-3d36-8fc0-780046513e81",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An entity or event with scope limited to a single region."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1a2fc4b-79b0-44b8-a875-5663889f8db8",
                                "sense_id": "c5cfa50e-35ab-343b-bdb8-9ec075d89186",
                                "text": "In the CPE^([Customer Premises Equipment]) market, all seven regionals are selling several sizes of private branch exchanges (PBX) and key systems for smaller customers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8b0c28d-a282-45d2-9bf6-d8379fa9b073",
                                "sense_id": "c5cfa50e-35ab-343b-bdb8-9ec075d89186",
                                "text": "Regionals are among the fastest growing companies and, as the name implies, are those carriers that for the most part provide service to only one region of the country and generate revenue of under $100 million."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0925cb03-480f-46e8-bf69-82564c579617",
                                "sense_id": "c5cfa50e-35ab-343b-bdb8-9ec075d89186",
                                "text": "Regional magazines are general interest publications for readers who live in a particular area of the country. Most major cities have their own regionals: New York, Chicago, Boston, Philadelphia, Kansas City, Miami […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
